%% Authentication state of an Azure File Sync deployment - shared key to managed identity and back - Contoso profile
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-file-sync-private-path.md and docs/RULES.md AFS-12 and AFS-19 (Microsoft Learn: How to use managed identities with Azure File Sync)
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB

  state "Shared key - UseIdentity False, server ActiveAuthType Certificate, LatestApplicationId empty" as SharedKey
  state "Server has an identity but is not using it - LatestApplicationId holds a GUID, ActiveAuthType still Certificate" as Ready
  state "Set-AzStorageSyncServiceIdentity running - several minutes, longer on large topologies" as Configuring
  state "Managed identity active - UseIdentity True, ApplicationId holds a GUID, ActiveAuthType ManagedIdentity" as MIActive
  state "New server registered later - it does NOT inherit the configuration and falls back to shared key" as NewServer
  state "Blocked - cross-tenant topology is unsupported, the server cannot connect" as Blocked
  state "Shared key can now be disabled for File Sync, but Azure Backup for Azure Files still requires allowSharedKeyAccess true" as KeyOptional

  [*] --> SharedKey
  SharedKey --> SharedKey : agent below 20.0.0.0 or no Arc, assessor reports AFS-12
  SharedKey --> Ready : agent 20.0.0.0 or later AND the server is Arc-enabled on-premises or an Azure VM with system-assigned identity
  Ready --> Blocked : Storage Sync Service, server resource, identity or role assignments in different Entra tenants
  Ready --> Configuring : operator holds Azure File Sync Administrator or Owner or roleassignments write, with Az.StorageSync 2.5.0 or later
  Configuring --> MIActive : grants Storage Account Contributor to the service identity on the storage accounts, Storage File Data Privileged Contributor to the service identity and to each server identity on the shares, then flips UseIdentity
  MIActive --> MIActive : up to 15 minutes before the server actually authenticates with the identity
  MIActive --> NewServer : a new Windows Server is registered with the Storage Sync Service
  NewServer --> Configuring : re-run Set-AzStorageSyncServiceIdentity or use Turn on Managed identity in the portal
  NewServer --> SharedKey : left unattended, the new server keeps using the account key, assessor reports AFS-19
  MIActive --> KeyOptional : every registered server shows ActiveAuthType ManagedIdentity
  KeyOptional --> [*]

  note right of SharedKey
    Contoso starting state on the File Sync accounts.
    SEC-04 stays open by design while this holds.
  end note

  note right of MIActive
    Verify with Get-AzStorageSyncService UseIdentity True
    and Get-AzStorageSyncServer ActiveAuthType ManagedIdentity.
    The private path over ExpressRoute is independent of this
    state - managed identity is recommended, not a prerequisite.
  end note

  note right of KeyOptional
    Setting allowSharedKeyAccess false here still breaks
    Azure Backup jobs and is the BKP-18 incident class.
  end note
